			"ChannelId": "UCiZeuI-7OPs7TmMel6Q5Msw",
			"ChannelTitle": "Kanishk Nishar",
			"Description": "Gustav Mahler \nSymphony No 6 \u0022Tragic\u0022\n\n1. Allegro energico, ma non troppo.\n   Heftig aber markig\n2. Andante moderato\n3. Scherzo.Wuchtig\n4. Finale. Allegro moderato-Allegro energico\n\nHermann Scherchen, conductor\nLeipzig Radio Symphony Orchestra\n\nRecorded Live in 1960\n\nScherchen, alas, did not leave a recording of the 6th symphony with the complete score. The present recording is from a live performance. His interpretation of the score is one of the fastest, but it is not without some extraordinary moments in musical terms. In  the 1950s and 60s a conductor was blazing New Trails with Mahler\u0027s lesser-known symphonies, and consensus was very different than it is today.\n\nThe symphony itself puzzled earlier audiences, and the origin of the \u0022Tragic\u0022 title is unclear. Mahler composed the symphony during one of the happiest times in his life. There has also been a controversy about the order of the inner movements. The present edition is in the more accepted order of \u0022Andante-Scherzo\u0022.\n\nAlthough critics and audiences were unconvinced at first, some, like Webern and Berg saw the 6th as a masterpiece. The symphony has become very popular over the last 40 years or so.",
